Drop the LuCI suffix from the Status - Overview "Firmware Version" line

The pinned luci feed checkout is in detached-HEAD state, so the LuCI build
stamps the git describe ("LuCI (HEAD detached at 128a7812) branch ...")
into the version modules and the status page renders it after the release
description. CleanWRT renders the release description alone:
"CleanWRT <version> <date>". The luci JS is MINIFIED at package build
time, so patching this readable source line is what removes the suffix
from the shipped minified file (validated against the built form on the
device). The luci identity stays visible in the page footer, the login
footer and `ubus call luci getVersion` via the version.lua / version.uc
overlays (files/usr/...), labelled "LuCI 25.12.5".

Applies to: https://git.openwrt.org/project/luci.git
            @ 350fc919675bb62e415927afff65697fcb8f775d (pinned in feeds.conf.default)
Applied by: tools/cw-apply-feed-patches.sh (patch -p1, zero fuzz - the build
            fails if upstream changes this line; re-port it then).
Upstream status: not submitted (CleanWRT-specific branding).

--- a/modules/luci-mod-status/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/status/include/10_system.js
+++ b/modules/luci-mod-status/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/status/include/10_system.js
@@ -68,5 +68,5 @@
 			_('Architecture'),     boardinfo.system,
 			_('Target Platform'),  (L.isObject(boardinfo.release) ? boardinfo.release.target : ''),
-			_('Firmware Version'), (L.isObject(boardinfo.release) ? boardinfo.release.description + ' / ' : '') + (luciversion || ''),
+			_('Firmware Version'), (L.isObject(boardinfo.release) ? boardinfo.release.description : ''),
 			_('Kernel Version'),   boardinfo.kernel,
 			_('Local Time'),       datestr,
